Z||000000||Pretender||10-22-1999||02:09 AM||||the other night(3 days ago) i was coming home from my girlfriends house and i decided to peg it but i only ended up hitting 115mph when i seen a car so i let off, when i did i heard a backfire(only one since i owned it,5 years) but i thought nothing of it. the next day on my way to work the car started hesitating and the tack whas jumping like crazy when i was at regular idle2500k-up(calm accelaration).. It goes away when i decide to accelerate at a harder pace. T haven't had time to take a look at it so i don't have a clue, it could be anything! i was thinking about checking the ing. system and maybe the throttle boddie . Anoyone else have this prob? thought i'd ask before the teardown. Thanks...<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||10-22-1999||04:18 AM||||Try removing the tachfilter first and see if the problem remains. If so, you've fried the ignition module. If not, your tachfilter needs to be replaced.||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||10-22-1999||03:38 PM||||Sounds like an ignition problem of some sort. A weak spark plug wire will even cause a hesitation and an occasional backfire. I'm speaking from experience on this one because that happened to me once on my 2.5L 87 SE.||||reg||1
